<mujoco model="2_joint_arm">
    <asset>
        <texture type="skybox" name="sky" builtin="flat" rgb1="0.75 0.9 1" rgb2="0.75 0.9 1"
            width="512"
            height="512" />
        <material name="sky_mat" texture="sky" />
    </asset>

    <option gravity="0 0 -9.81" />

    <worldbody>
        <geom type="plane" size="10 10 1" rgba="0.969 0.969 0.957 1" />
        <camera name="main" pos="0 5 1" />

        <!-- has no child joints therefore treated as welded to the world -->
        <body name="base" pos="0 0 0">
            <geom type="cylinder" size="0.05 0.4" pos="0 0 0.4" rgba="0.5 0.5 0.5 1" />
        </body>

        <body name="first-arm-body" pos="0 0 0.8">
            <joint name="shoulder" type="hinge" axis="1 0 0" />
            <geom type="capsule" size="0.045" fromto="0 0 0 0 0 -0.43" density="1000" rgba="1 0 0 1" />

            <body name="fore-arm-body" pos="0 0 -0.43">
                <joint name="elbow" type="hinge" axis="1 0 0" />
                <geom type="capsule" size="0.04" fromto="0 0 0 0 0.3 0" density="1000"
                    rgba="0 1 0 1" />

                <body name="hand" pos="0 0.3 0">
                    <geom type="sphere" size="0.04" density="1000" rgba="0 0 1 1" />
                </body>
            </body>
        </body>
    </worldbody>

    <actuator>
        <motor joint="shoulder" gear="10" />
        <motor joint="elbow" gear="10" />
    </actuator>
</mujoco>

<!-- 
Official Geom Types
- plane (mjGEOM_PLANE): An infinite 2D surface, commonly used as the ground
- hfield (mjGEOM_HFIELD): Height field, useful for terrain generation by referencing an elevation
asset
- sphere (mjGEOM_SPHERE): A basic spherical shape
- capsule (mjGEOM_CAPSULE): A cylinder with hemispherical ends. Very common for limb segments in
robotics and characters
- ellipsoid (mjGEOM_ELLIPSOID): A scaled 3D sphere... (thickness, width, length)
- cylinder (mjGEOM_CYLINDER): A standard cylinder
- box (mjGEOM_BOX): A rectangular prism (cuboid)
- mesh (mjGEOM_MESH): Complex 3D models imported from asset files (e.g., STL, OBJ)
- sdf (mjGEOM_SDF): Signed Distance Field for complex geometry-collision handling

Geom fromto: defines the spatial orientation and length of a geometric primitive
by specifying its start and end coordinates. It takes six real numbers in the format fromto="x1 y1
z1 x2 y2 z2", which overrides the default position (pos) and orientation (quat) parameters for
select shapes.

start (x1, y1, z1) to end (x2, y2, z2)
(x1, y1), (x2, y2), (x3, y3)

ex. Capsule from (0, 0, 0) to (0, 0, 1) with radius 0.1
    <geom type="capsule" size="0.1" fromto="0 0 0 0 0 1"/>

This means:
z
1 ●
|
|
|
0 ●

fromto="0 0 0 1 0 0" would be
x
●────────●
0        1



Understanding Coordinates of Camera and Bodies:
Think that each body has its own (x, y, z) coordinates

World

        Z
        ^
        |
        |
        O ....> X
       /
      Y

        y
        ^
        |
        |
        O ....> x
       /
      z

WHen you write <body pos="1 0 0">, you are saying that everything inside that body is relative to
(1, 0, 0) which is its origin.
-->